# CR 707.10: a copy of a spell copies "the value of X". Bot1 casts Devastating Onslaught for X=1 targeting Mox Sapphire, and in
# response flashes in Lutri, the Spellchaser (Black Lotus's {R}{R}{R}), whose trigger copies the Onslaught; Bot1 keeps the copy's
# target. The copy resolves first with X=1 and makes one Mox Sapphire token; then the original makes another: two tokens,
# not one (a copy with X=0 would make none). Both are sacrificed at the end step, leaving the original Sapphire.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Devastating Onslaught
Lutri, the Spellchaser
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Devastating Onslaught.Cast(Mox Sapphire; X: 1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Lutri, the Spellchaser.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 6
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Mox Emerald; Mox Sapphire; Lutri, the Spellchaser
Bot1.Graveyard = Devastating Onslaught; Black Lotus
Stack.Count = 0
